# `scripts/` used to be blanket-ignored here. Removed 2026-08-30: it is
# developer tooling that belongs with the code -- notably the oracle-capture
# scripts, whose whole value is that a reader can see how a fixture was made.
# The rule was also a footgun: with no leading slash it matched at ANY depth
# and had already swallowed package source under klotho/ once (hence the
# klotho/**/scripts/ negations below, which it made necessary).
# (Caches there are already covered by the **/__pycache__/ rule at the top.)
ut_plotter/
.taskmaster/
benchmarks/
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md
TUTORIALS_WORKFLOW.md
build_and_upload.sh
build_and_upload_test.sh
rebuild_tutorials.sh
klotho-book/

# ==========================
# Tracked exceptions
# ==========================

!tests/
!tests/**
tests/**/__pycache__/

# Examples directory (tracked, currently empty)
!examples/
!examples/.gitkeep

# Tutorials directory (tracked, currently empty)
!tutorials/
!tutorials/.gitkeep

# SuperSonic assets (always tracked)
!klotho/utils/playback/supersonic/assets/**/*.scd
klotho/utils/playback/supersonic/assets/foxdot_random_tester.scd
klotho/utils/playback/supersonic/assets/synthdef_tester.scd
!klotho/utils/playback/supersonic/assets/**/*.scsyndef
!klotho/utils/playback/supersonic/assets/manifest.json
!klotho/utils/playback/supersonic/assets/kinds.json
!klotho/utils/playback/supersonic/assets/samples/samples.json

# Package source swept up by the blanket rules above. These are shipped
# modules and data, not local artifacts: `*.json` caught two data files and
# the top-level `scripts/` rule matches at any depth, so it swallowed an
# in-package module. Tracked so the tracked set matches the shipped set --
# MANIFEST.in reads the working tree, not git.
!klotho/utils/data_structures/8th-octave.json
!klotho/utils/playback/supersonic/scripts/
!klotho/utils/playback/supersonic/scripts/*.py

# Graphify knowledge graph
graphify-out/

# Local analysis / tooling artifacts
.understand-anything/
*_UX_AUDIT.md

.claude-tmp/

# ==========================
# Package source is never ignored
# ==========================
# The blanket rules above -- bare `*.json`, and `scripts/` with no leading
# slash so it matches at any depth -- are meant for the working tree, not for
# the distributed package. Both have already swallowed shipped package source
# once: API-R (2026-08-28) found four files that MANIFEST.in was shipping from
# the working tree because git had never tracked them.
#
# These negations are scoped to `klotho/` on purpose. Narrowing the rules
# themselves would change what is ignored across the whole tree, which is a
# larger change than this footgun warrants.
!klotho/**/*.json
!klotho/**/scripts/
!klotho/**/scripts/**

# ...but the negations above must not drag caches back in.
klotho/**/__pycache__/
klotho/**/*.py[cod]
